{
    "background_story": "Amina was a young entrepreneur from Zambia who had a passion for innovation. Growing up, she was fascinated by the concept of ngwee, the smallest unit of currency in Zambia. She saw how the value of ngwee could add up to make a big difference in people's lives. Amina created a mobile app that allowed users to save and invest their ngwee, making it easier for low-income individuals to manage their finances. Her app quickly gained popularity, and soon she was able to expand her services to other countries. Amina's determination to empower others through financial inclusion earned her recognition as a leading innovator in Africa. Her story is a testament to the power of small beginnings and the impact one person can have on their community.",
